proposed_rollup_levels:
1) raw-token -- keep dims: request_id, tenant_id, model_variant, region, kv_cache_hit;
2) session -- keep dims: session_id, tenant_id, route, model_family, avg_seq_len;
3) route -- keep dims: route_name, model_family, region, bucketed_seq_len;
4) tenant -- keep dims: tenant_id, service_tier;
5) global -- keep dims: region, model_family.
Guideline: drop ephemeral/dense tags at each level and cap dimension cardinality by design (e.g., top 100 tenants exposed).

latency_budget_table:
raw-token: target p50 < 30ms, p95 < 50ms;
session: p50 < 60ms, p95 < 100ms;
route: p95 < 150ms;
tenant: p95 < 200ms;
global: p99 < 300ms.
Notes: budgets are intentionally conservative at low levels to make regressions localizable; budgets should be tuned per-model-family in follow-up work.
